---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ProgressControls from '../components/ProgressControls.astro';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';

const modules = await getCollection('course');

// Curriculum block order from data/curriculum/CURRICULUM.md (main-route order, not alphabetical).
const BLOCK_ORDER = ['MATH', 'OPT', 'PROB', 'ODE', 'KIN', 'DYN', 'PLAN', 'MANIP', 'ML', 'RL', 'SYM', 'RLEARN', 'CAP'];
const sorted = [...modules].sort((a, b) => {
  const bi = BLOCK_ORDER.indexOf(a.data.block) - BLOCK_ORDER.indexOf(b.data.block);
  return bi !== 0 ? bi : a.data.id.localeCompare(b.data.id);
});
const totalHours = modules.reduce((sum, m) => sum + m.data.estimatedHours, 0);
---
<BaseLayout title="Start Here">
  <h1>Toussaint Workbook</h1>
  <p>
    A private, self-paced course built from Marc Toussaint's TU Berlin lecture notes, sequenced and
    prioritized for one specific PhD research direction. {modules.length} of ~63 planned modules are
    authored so far (~{totalHours} hrs), produced in batches per <code>data/curriculum/CURRICULUM.md</code>.
  </p>

  <h2>Modules so far</h2>
  <ul>
    {sorted.map((m) => (
      <li>
        <a href={`/course/${m.data.block}/${m.data.id}`}><strong>{m.data.id}</strong>: {m.data.title}</a>
        {' '}<span style="opacity:0.6">(~{m.data.estimatedHours} hrs, block {m.data.block})</span>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ul>

  <h2>My progress</h2>
  <p>
    Your answers and check results are saved automatically in this browser as you use the site (see
    "Where your answers live" below). Use these to back up or move your progress to another browser or
    machine.
  </p>
  <ProgressControls />

  <h2>Where your answers live</h2>
  <p>
    Everything you type into an exercise, and every check/attempt result, is saved locally in this
    browser's storage (IndexedDB) the moment you click "Check", "I've attempted this", or the review
    button. Nothing is sent to a server: this site has no backend and no database of its own.
  </p>
  <p>
    That means: progress is tied to <em>this browser on this machine</em>. It will not appear in a
    different browser, a different machine, or if someone clones the underlying git repository: no
    progress data is ever written into a file that git tracks, so cloning the code gives zero access to
    your answers. Clearing this browser's site data (or using a private/incognito window) will erase
    progress for this site, so use "Export my progress" above to keep a backup, or before switching
    machines.
  </p>

  <h2>Full curriculum</h2>
  <p>
    The complete 13-block, ~63-module plan lives in <code>data/curriculum/CURRICULUM.md</code>: not yet
    wired into this site's navigation as a roadmap page, since most modules aren't authored yet. The
    roadmap/search/index pages described in <code>data/curriculum/ARCHITECTURE.md</code> get built once
    enough real content exists to make them worthwhile.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
